   "html_text": "This implicit difference in how Dai interprets the dao results in his distinct methodology and his dissatisfaction with the academic climate of his day. For Dai’s contemporaries, the dao is the institutions the sages established to govern the world. For Dai, the dao is the philosophy or guiding principles the sages applied in creating these institutions. However, we may question the scope of the understanding of the Classics that Dai demands. For example, to understand the sages’ guiding princip",
